2026-09-14  Licensing System — Full Seller/Customer Lifecycle Implementation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CONTEXT
  Reviewed the complete licensing system from the perspective of a software
  seller and customers (hotels/restaurants). Mapped every real-world scenario:
  new sale, 6-month plan, 1-year plan, renewal, upgrade, revoke, and expiry.
  Identified gaps and implemented all critical missing pieces.

CHANGES MADE

  electron/licensing.cjs
    - Added 7-day grace period after license expiry (app still works, badge shown)
    - Throws 'EXPIRED' (machine-readable) instead of human string when past grace
    - getLicenseStatus() now extracts expiresAt from blob even on failure, so
      ActivationScreen can show the actual expiry date in the error message
    - activateLicense() now maps 'EXPIRED' throw to a human-readable message:
      "This license has expired. Contact the vendor to renew before activating."
    - payload.gracePeriodDaysLeft is set (days remaining in grace) when in grace

  electron/main.cjs
    - Added hourly setInterval recheck of license status after app starts
    - If license transitions to invalid (e.g. customer applies a revoked blob),
      app relaunches automatically into the Activation screen
    - Only runs for HOST/standalone installs; Client terminals are never gated

  src/App.jsx
    - Added expiryBannerDismissed state (persisted in sessionStorage)
    - Added showExpiryBanner computed value: true when <=14 days until expiry
      and not in grace period (grace is handled by ActivationScreen instead)
    - Added dismissible yellow warning banner at top of app shell:
      "Your license expires on [date] — contact your vendor to renew."
      Changes to "only Nd left!" when <=7 days remain

  src/components/Settings/LicenseInfoSection.jsx  [NEW FILE]
    - In-app license information panel shown in Settings page
    - Displays: Licensed hotel name, modules (Food Billing / Room Booking badges),
      issued date, expiry date with color-coded status badge, Machine ID
    - Status badges: Perpetual (blue), green (>30d), yellow (<=30d), red (<=7d),
      grace (amber), expired (red)
    - Only rendered in Electron desktop (window.api present); hidden on mobile

  src/components/Settings/SettingsPage.jsx
    - Imported LicenseInfoSection
    - Added <LicenseInfoSection> before the "Files & Records" section

  src/index.css
    - Added .license-info-grid, .license-info-row, .license-info-label,
      .license-info-value, .license-info-machineid, .license-info-no-payload
    - Added .license-module-badge (green pill for module names)
    - Added .license-expiry-badge + variants: perpetual/green/yellow/red/grace/expired
    - Added .expiry-warning-banner and .expiry-warning-banner-dismiss

  license-dashboard/server.cjs
    - Added POST /api/licenses/:id/revoke route
    - Revoke re-issues the license with expiresAt = yesterday
    - Customer's app blocks access on next hourly recheck or restart once
      they apply the new (expired) blob

  license-dashboard/public/app.js
    - Added "Revoke" button (amber) to each license row
    - Revoke handler: POST /revoke → shows new expired blob in result overlay
      with message explaining customer must apply it to be blocked
    - Updated Delete confirmation text to clearly state it only removes the
      vendor history record and does NOT revoke access on customer machine
    - Result overlay heading + hint text now reset correctly when opening for
      generate/extend vs revoke (previously could show stale "Revoked" heading)

  license-dashboard/public/style.css
    - Added .btn-link.btn-revoke (amber color for the Revoke button)

  docs/licensing.md  [NEW FILE]
    - Full reference documentation for the licensing system
    - Covers: architecture, payload structure, module tiers, file locations,
      vendor workflow, all seller/customer scenarios, grace period table,
      feature status table, known gaps, future TO-DO list, data flow diagram

SCENARIO COVERAGE (as of this session)

  Seller scenarios:
    ✅ Issue new license (6-month, 1-year, perpetual)
    ✅ Renew / extend expiry
    ✅ Upgrade or downgrade modules
    ✅ Revoke access (re-issue expired blob)
    ✅ Delete from vendor history (dashboard only, does not affect customer)

  Customer scenarios:
    ✅ First activation from unlicensed state
    ✅ Normal use within license period
    ✅ 14-day advance expiry warning banner (dismissible)
    ✅ 7-day grace period after expiry (app still works, badge shown in Settings)
    ✅ Auto-relaunch to Activation screen when grace ends
    ✅ Activation screen shows actual expiry date when expired
    ✅ Clear error when trying to activate an expired blob
    ✅ In-app Settings panel showing all license details
    ✅ Module restrictions (food-only, rooms-only, both)
    ✅ Wrong machine detection with clear message
    ✅ Multi-terminal: Client terminals bypass license check entirely

KNOWN GAPS (offline-first design trade-offs)
    ⚠️  Revoke requires customer to apply the new blob (cannot push remotely)
    ⚠️  No usage reporting (no server)
    ⚠️  No concurrent-user or seat count enforcement

