2026-09-14  Mobile/Android App — Alignment with Desktop Changes
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GAPS FIXED IN src/mobile/webApi.js

  1. CRITICAL — Discount stored on every room in group (was multiplying discount by N rooms)
     Fix: discount: idx === 0 ? payload.discount || 0 : 0  (same as desktop)

  2. HIGH — Early group check-in blocked on mobile
     Fix: Added sibling room check in checkInBooking() — if any sibling is
     CHECKED_IN/CHECKED_OUT, allow early check-in and advance the date to today

  3. HIGH — Early group check-out blocked on mobile
     Fix: Same sibling check added to checkOutBooking()

  4. HIGH — Sibling rooms hidden when filtering bookings by date
     Fix: After main filter, fetch all bookings sharing same bookingGroupId
     that were excluded by the date filter (drop date filter for siblings,
     keep status filter) — matches db/roomService.cjs listBookings logic

  5. MINOR — nights() used full datetime strings (fragile near midnight/timezone)
     Fix: Slices to date-only (YYYY-MM-DD) before constructing Date objects,
     matching db/roomService.cjs exactly

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-09-14  Vite Port Detection — Fix for Port Collision on Restart
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PROBLEM
  When Electron dev is restarted while old processes still hold port 5173,
  Vite increments to 5174, 5175, etc. The old wait-on command required ALL
  listed ports to respond (they never do), so Electron never launched.

CHANGES MADE

  scripts/wait-vite.cjs  [NEW FILE]
    - Polls ports 5173-5185 every 300ms
    - Exits as soon as ANY one port answers (first-match, not all-match)
    - Timeout 30s with clear error if nothing responds

  package.json
    - electron:wait now uses: node scripts/wait-vite.cjs && cross-env ...
    - Replaced the multi-port wait-on command

  electron/main.cjs
    - Added global.VITE_PORT_READY promise that probes ports 5173-5185 in parallel
    - global.VITE_PORT is set to whichever port answers first
    - app.whenReady() now awaits global.VITE_PORT_READY before createMainWindow()
    - All loadURL() calls use ${global.VITE_PORT || 5173}

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-09-13  Group Bookings — Full Feature Implementation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

FEATURES ADDED

  Group booking sibling display in Bookings tab
    - listBookings() now fetches all sibling rooms sharing booking_group_id
      even when their check-in dates fall outside the current date filter
    - E.g. filtering "Today" for a group booked across Sep 14/15/16 shows all
      three rooms, not just the one matching the date filter

  Early check-in/check-out for group siblings
    - checkIn() and checkOut() now allow early action if at least one sibling
      in the group is already CHECKED_IN or CHECKED_OUT
    - Check-in date is automatically advanced to today in both cases

  Discount fix for group bookings
    - createBooking() was writing payload.discount to every room row
    - computeRoomCharge() deducts discount per room, causing N× overbilling
    - Fix: discount stored only on idx===0 (master room), 0 on all others
    - advancePayment was already correctly stored on master room only

  BookingsTab.jsx frontend
    - blockFuture check now accounts for group siblings being active
    - "Check In" button enabled for future-dated rooms when group siblings active

  Seed data (scripts/seed-demo-data.cjs)  [NEW FILE]
    - Seeds representative demo data covering all fixed bug scenarios:
      same-day turnover, group invoices, advance payments, night count,
      oversized discounts, ID row presence, early group check-in scenario

  Edge case tests (scripts/edge-case-test.cjs)
    - Added Section 7 with 4 new tests:
      1. SQLite datetime format mismatch (space vs T separator)
      2. Combined invoice gate (blocked when any room still pending)
      3. Advance payment cap (advance > charge → bill total >= 0)
      4. Discount + advance sum (combined never produces negative bill)

